SUMMARY:Film: In the Mood for Love (2000)
DESCRIPTION:Wong Kar-wai · 98 min\n\nTwo neighbours in 1960s Hong Kong dis
 cover their spouses are having an affair\, and slowly fall for each other 
 without acting on it. It is one of the most beautiful films ever made\, wi
 th its slow motion\, cheongsam dresses and repeated waltz theme. It shows 
 how much can be said through restraint.\n\nAfter: What does the film sugge
 st about the cost of always doing the 'proper' thing?\n\nWhere to watch: h
 ttps://www.justwatch.com/uk/search?q=In%20the%20Mood%20for%20Love
URL:https://www.justwatch.com/uk/search?q=In%20the%20Mood%20for%20Love
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
